# Linguini's history starts with one commit whose parent is `base`, so upstream history is shared
# and merges have a normal merge base. To sync:
#   git remote add upstream https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code.git; git fetch upstream main
#   git merge upstream/main
# Then update base= and synced= above.
# Linguini does not carry upstream's GitHub automation: .github/workflows (except our own
# linguini-ci.yml), .github/actions, .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE, .github/pull_request_template.md,
# .github/VOUCHED.td, .github/TRIAGE_EXEMPTIONS.td and scripts/notify-discord-release.test.ts
# (it reads release.yml) were deleted, and .github/SECURITY.md is ours. When a sync reports a
# modify/delete conflict on one of these, keep it deleted:
#   git status --short | awk '$1=="DU"||$1=="UD"{print $2}' | grep -E '^(\.github/|scripts/notify-discord-release\.test\.ts$)' | xargs -r git rm -q
# and keep ours on content conflicts in .github/SECURITY.md (git checkout --ours -- .github/SECURITY.md).
# New upstream files under .github/workflows arrive as additions: delete them too (git rm) unless wanted.
